{{define "time-budget"}}{{with .Budget}}{{if .Duration}}TIME BUDGET
You have {{minutes .Duration}} of wall-clock time, until {{.Deadline.Format "15:04:05"}} UTC
(run `date -u` to check the time). Conclave then stops you, and a run stopped
before it prints its JSON object counts as failed: nothing you found reaches
the result. Organize your work for that budget:
- Start with what matters most and spend your time where problems are
  likely; do not dwell on what you can judge at a glance.
- Read each file once, by line ranges, and only the parts you need.
- Run independent reads and searches together rather than one at a time.
- Once about three quarters of the budget is spent, stop exploring and write
  the JSON object with what you have verified by then. A shorter answer
  delivered in time is worth more than a complete one that never arrives.

